WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the spoken Hinglish, not a verbatim transcript. Cue timing is automatically aligned and is not human-verified; it can still be wrong.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.260 line:0% position:50% align:center
Hi everyone! Batch 1 covers the basics of Travelling
Allowance, or TA,

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.300 line:0% position:50% align:center
in simple Hinglish.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:11.880 line:0% position:50% align:center
TA concerns travel costs for official duty; it is not

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.780 line:0% position:50% align:center
payment for every personal trip.

5
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:18.040 line:0% position:50% align:center
Suppose a Delhi employee goes to Jaipur for an office
inspection:

6
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.240 line:0% position:50% align:center
check TA under the rules for the approved trip.

7
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.220 line:0% position:50% align:center
But if the same employee takes a weekend trip with family,

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.720 line:0% position:50% align:center
that is not an official tour.

9
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.120 line:0% position:50% align:center
Another important point: TA and LTC are not the same.

10
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.040 line:0% position:50% align:center
The Department of Expenditure issues Central civilian TA
orders;

11
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.620 line:0% position:50% align:center
check DoPT guidelines for LTC and service rules too.

12
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.380 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, official training travel and a home-town holiday
claim

13
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.480 line:0% position:50% align:center
are two different cases.

14
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.740 line:0% position:50% align:center
Railways and the Armed Forces may have separate orders, so
check

15
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.280 line:0% position:50% align:center
the rules for your service.

16
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.520 line:0% position:50% align:center
Now the dates. The main TA order was issued on 13 July 2017,

17
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:59.680 line:0% position:50% align:center
but the changes took effect from 1 July 2017.

18
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.920 line:0% position:50% align:center
For a trip completed on 30 June, check the old rules; for a 2
July

19
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.260 line:0% position:50% align:center
trip, start with the new rules.

20
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.240 line:0% position:50% align:center
The issue date and effective date are not the same.

21
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.410 line:0% position:50% align:center
Now check protection of old entitlements. If the new order
reduces

22
00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:19.730 line:0% position:50% align:center
a person's or group's existing travel class or mode, the
saving clause

23
00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:24.050 line:0% position:50% align:center
continues the earlier, higher entitlement until, in the normal
course,

24
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.970 line:0% position:50% align:center
a higher entitlement becomes available.

25
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:30.830 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, if an officer's earlier approved class was better
than the new table,

26
00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.770 line:0% position:50% align:center
ask the office to check the saving clause and earlier proof.

27
00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:36.830 line:0% position:50% align:center
This does not mean an automatic upgrade for every employee.

28
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.480 line:0% position:50% align:center
TA entitlement depends on Pay Level; Pay Level and the pay

29
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.240 line:0% position:50% align:center
amount are not the same thing.

30
00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.240 line:0% position:50% align:center
In the 2017 order, Pay in the Level means basic pay in the
matrix level;

31
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.800 line:0% position:50% align:center
NPA, MSP or special pay are not added to that definition.

32
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.160 line:0% position:50% align:center
Suppose basic pay is Rs 50,000 and NPA is Rs 10,000:

33
00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.400 line:0% position:50% align:center
under this definition, pay is Rs 50,000, not Rs 60,000.

34
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.150 line:0% position:50% align:center
Another example: a Level 7 employee checks travel class

35
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.570 line:0% position:50% align:center
in the Level 6 to 11 row.

36
00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:09.010 line:0% position:50% align:center
But each TA component may be calculated differently.

37
00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:12.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not decide the transfer-grant amount from the travel-class
table alone;

38
00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.130 line:0% position:50% align:center
check that component's separate conditions.

39
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
For domestic official tour or training, the travel class

40
00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.840 line:0% position:50% align:center
is determined by Pay Level.

41
00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:26.060 line:0% position:50% align:center
Level 14 and above: business/club air or AC First by train;

42
00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.980 line:0% position:50% align:center
Levels 12 and 13: economy air or AC First.

43
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:34.760 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, Level 13A receives Level 13 treatment for TA and
Daily Allowance;

44
00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.480 line:0% position:50% align:center
the letter A alone does not confer business class.

45
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.200 line:0% position:50% align:center
Trip approval and booking rules also matter.

46
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.370 line:0% position:50% align:center
Levels 6 to 11: economy air or AC Second by train; Level 5 and

47
00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:50.250 line:0% position:50% align:center
below: First Class, AC Third or AC Chair Car by train.

48
00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.710 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a Level 7 employee on an approved official tour

49
00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.270 line:0% position:50% align:center
may be entitled to an economy flight.

50
00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:59.850 line:0% position:50% align:center
But ordinary LTC does not give Levels 6 to 8 the same air
entitlement;

51
00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:03.370 line:0% position:50% align:center
some special LTC schemes may differ.

52
00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.430 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not mix tour rules with LTC.

53
00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.660 line:0% position:50% align:center
There is a separate table for some premium trains, including
Rajdhani, Shatabdi,

54
00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.340 line:0% position:50% align:center
Duronto, Premium, Premium Tatkal and Suvidha.

55
00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.420 line:0% position:50% align:center
Level 12 and above: Executive or AC First; Levels 6 to 11: AC
Second

56
00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:23.060 line:0% position:50% align:center
or Shatabdi Chair Car; Level 5 and below: AC Third or

57
00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.400 line:0% position:50% align:center
Chair Car, subject to the table.

58
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.890 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a Level 7 employee checks Shatabdi Chair Car
entitlement,

59
00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:32.010 line:0% position:50% align:center
rather than assuming Executive class.

60
00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:36.610 line:0% position:50% align:center
For Premium Tatkal charges and Shatabdi, Rajdhani and Duronto
dynamic or flexi

61
00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:41.190 line:0% position:50% align:center
fares, check the order's exact wording; fixed-fare Tatkal Seva
charges also

62
00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:45.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
continue. For example, when claiming an eligible Shatabdi
dynamic fare,

63
00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.220 line:0% position:50% align:center
check the order's conditions.

64
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:52.170 line:0% position:50% align:center
Now the 2023 train update. Tejas and Vande Bharat follow

65
00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.490 line:0% position:50% align:center
Shatabdi entitlement; Humsafar follows Rajdhani.

66
00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:58.670 line:0% position:50% align:center
Check this mapping for the listed tour, training, transfer

67
00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.310 line:0% position:50% align:center
