00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.630 line:0% position:50% align:center
food, transfer or LTC claim.

176
00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:54.020 line:0% position:50% align:center
For an intercity road journey, first check whether the
concerned State or

177
00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:57.080 line:0% position:50% align:center
a neighbouring State Transport Directorate has prescribed
specific

178
00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:58.700 line:0% position:50% align:center
rates.

179
00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:03.550 line:0% position:50% align:center
If rates are prescribed, check the eligible mode and Pay Level
conditions.

180
00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:08.110 line:0% position:50% align:center
Example: an employee checks the vehicle entitlement and the
rail-connected

181
00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:10.450 line:0% position:50% align:center
route fare condition for the road journey.

182
00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:15.500 line:0% position:50% align:center
An available taxi does not entitle every Pay Level to every
taxi class.

183
00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.880 line:0% position:50% align:center
Do not mix this with the tour-station city-travel daily
ceiling.

184
00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:23.130 line:0% position:50% align:center
Where neither relevant Transport Directorate has prescribed
rates,

185
00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:27.950 line:0% position:50% align:center
the 2017 fallback was Rs 24 for own car or taxi and Rs 12 for
auto or own

186
00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.230 line:0% position:50% align:center
scooter per kilometre.

187
00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:34.300 line:0% position:50% align:center
After the first 25% increase these become Rs 30 and Rs 15.

188
00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:38.760 line:0% position:50% align:center
Example: an otherwise eligible, approved own-car journey is 40

189
00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:42.240 line:0% position:50% align:center
kilometres; multiplying by Rs 30 gives Rs 1,200

190
00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
as a starting calculation.

191
00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:47.580 line:0% position:50% align:center
This calculation does not override vehicle entitlement, route
rules

192
00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.420 line:0% position:50% align:center
or other conditions.

193
00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:55.020 line:0% position:50% align:center
A TA claim for tour, transfer or training normally must be
submitted

194
00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:59.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
within 60 days after the journey; a late claim may be
forfeited,

195
00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.080 line:0% position:50% align:center
meaning lost.

196
00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:05.320 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, if the journey ends on 1 October 2026, then

197
00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:09.000 line:0% position:50% align:center
2 October is day one and 30 November is day 60.

198
00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.860 line:0% position:50% align:center
Submit on time to the correct office and keep proof.

199
00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:15.700 line:0% position:50% align:center
For retirement TA, the 2021 order set a limit of 180 days

200
00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:20.240 line:0% position:50% align:center
after the journey; tour, transfer and training remain at 60
days.

201
00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:24.540 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, if an eligible retirement journey ends on 1
October 2026,

202
00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:28.180 line:0% position:50% align:center
day 180 is 30 March 2027.

203
00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:32.880 line:0% position:50% align:center
Remember: the period allowed to make a journey and the
claim-filing deadline

204
00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:37.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
are different. The guide discusses possible review of old
unsettled cases.

205
00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:42.040 line:0% position:50% align:center
If an employee and family travel separately on transfer,

206
00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:44.440 line:0% position:50% align:center
the claim clock starts separately for each journey.

207
00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:49.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, the employee arrives on 1 October and the family
on 11 October;

208
00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.720 line:0% position:50% align:center
their completion dates are counted separately.

209
00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:55.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
For personal effects or conveyance, separately check the
actual delivery

210
00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:56.840 line:0% position:50% align:center
date at the new station.

211
00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:01.410 line:0% position:50% align:center
When a claim is considered submitted also depends on whether

212
00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:03.670 line:0% position:50% align:center
you are your own controlling officer.

213
00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:07.730 line:0% position:50% align:center
If not, check the submission date to the Head of Office or
controlling officer;

214
00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:11.250 line:0% position:50% align:center
if you are your own controlling officer, check the
presentation date

215
00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:12.830 line:0% position:50% align:center
at the Treasury or Cash Section.

216
00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:17.010 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, you submit to your controlling officer on day 45,

217
00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:20.530 line:0% position:50% align:center
and Treasury receives it later: subject to the order's
conditions,

218
00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:22.090 line:0% position:50% align:center
the earlier submission date may matter.

219
00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.290 line:0% position:50% align:center
Keep the receipt or acknowledgement safe.

220
00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:29.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
Quick official update: what if a boarding pass is missing? The
2020 DoE

221
00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:33.800 line:0% position:50% align:center
order applies to official tour journeys by Central Government
employees.

222
00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:38.000 line:0% position:50% align:center
If neither a physical nor a digital copy is available, the
prescribed declaration

223
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.820 line:0% position:50% align:center
may be submitted with the TA bill.

224
00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:45.050 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a Level 9 employee loses the pass and declares
the actual journey,

225
00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:48.590 line:0% position:50% align:center
PNR details and that the claim is not duplicated.

226
00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.610 line:0% position:50% align:center
Employees at Level 10 and below must have the declaration

227
00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:53.260 line:0% position:50% align:center
countersigned by the controlling officer.

228
00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:58.150 line:0% position:50% align:center
This missing-pass declaration differs from the
journey-completion certificate. The June

229
00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:01.690 line:0% position:50% align:center
2022 order requires the completion certificate within 72

230
00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:05.920 line:0% position:50% align:center
hours of the journey; the TA bill is submitted later under
separate rules.

231
00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:10.390 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, an employee sends the completion certificate
after a flight. If the

232
00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:14.270 line:0% position:50% align:center
boarding pass is missing, they attach the separate prescribed
declaration to the bill.

233
00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:17.630 line:0% position:50% align:center
A false declaration may lead to disciplinary action and
recovery.

234
00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:23.860 line:0% position:50% align:center
Transfer TA has four heads: travel for the employee and
eligible family,

235
00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:28.520 line:0% position:50% align:center
Composite Transfer Grant, or CTG, personal effects and
eligible

236
00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:30.050 line:0% position:50% align:center
conveyance transport.

237
00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:35.500 line:0% position:50% align:center
Example: on an approved public-interest transfer, the employee
checks family

238
00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:39.650 line:0% position:50% align:center
travel, belongings and vehicle in separate rows.

239
00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:44.000 line:0% position:50% align:center
Approval of one head does not automatically approve the other
three.

240
00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:48.690 line:0% position:50% align:center
Under the 2017 transfer order, if stations are 20 kilometres

241
00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:52.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
or more apart, subject to stated conditions, CTG is

242
00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:53.800 line:0% position:50% align:center
80% of last basic pay.

243
00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:59.010 line:0% position:50% align:center
Example: on an eligible transfer, last basic pay is Rs 50,000,
so

244
00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:02.350 line:0% position:50% align:center
80%, or Rs 40,000, is checked as CTG.

245
00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:06.900 line:0% position:50% align:center
For the same city or a distance under 20 kilometres, if the
residence actually changes,

246
00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:11.040 line:0% position:50% align:center
check the stated one-third rule. Restrictions for own-request
and spouse

247
00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:15.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
transfers differ; the 2022 retirement amendment is separate.

248
00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:19.610 line:0% position:50% align:center
From 1 January 2026, Dearness Allowance is 60%.

249
00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:24.120 line:0% position:50% align:center
When it rises from 50% to 60%, eligible TA rates do not get

250
00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:26.020 line:0% position:50% align:center
another automatic 25% increase.

251
00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:29.290 line:0% position:50% align:center
The first revision applies from January 2024.

252
00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:34.170 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, the road transport rate for Level 6 and above

253
00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:38.330 line:0% position:50% align:center
personal effects rose from Rs 50 to Rs 62.50 per kilometre;

254
00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.860 line:0% position:50% align:center
check the conditions for the actual claim.

255
00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:42.260 line:0% position:50% align:center
Now an important transfer exception.

256
00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:46.950 line:0% position:50% align:center
From or to the North East, Andaman and Nicobar, Lakshadweep or
Ladakh,

257
00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:51.470 line:0% position:50% align:center
if the family does not accompany the employee on transfer,

258
00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:54.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
up to one-third of the personal-effects entitlement may be
carried, and

259
00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:56.230 line:0% position:50% align:center
a receipt is not mandatory for that one-third claim.

260
00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:59.880 line:0% position:50% align:center
If family accompanies, a receipt is required for the
admissible amount.

261
00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:04.010 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, one-third of Level 7's 6,000 kg rail entitlement

262
00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:07.010 line:0% position:50% align:center
is up to 2,000 kg; check the other conditions as well.

263
00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:11.640 line:0% position:50% align:center
For technical resignation, see DoPT's 2022 consolidated order.

264
00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:16.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
If an employee applies through the proper channel for a
Government post, is selected

265
00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:20.180 line:0% position:50% align:center
and must resign for administrative reasons, under the stated
conditions

266
00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:21.760 line:0% position:50% align:center
it may be treated as technical.

267
00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:25.840 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, an employee is selected for another Government
post through

268
00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:30.420 line:0% position:50% align:center
the approved channel and resigns as required. Past service or
other benefits

269
00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.440 line:0% position:50% align:center
depend on the conditions of separate rules.

270
00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.940 line:0% position:50% align:center
Calling every resignation technical does not make benefits
automatic.

271
00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:40.430 line:0% position:50% align:center
In paragraph 3.6.3 of the same order, appointment through open
competition or

272
00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:42.970 line:0% position:50% align:center
interview to a Central Government post is subject to

273
00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:45.010 line:0% position:50% align:center
a specific transfer-TA rule.

274
00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:48.270 line:0% position:50% align:center
In that case, a temporary Central Government employee with
regular continuous

275
00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:52.870 line:0% position:50% align:center
service of under three years is not entitled to transfer TA.
For permanent or

276
00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:56.190 line:0% position:50% align:center
provisionally permanent State employees, check the paragraph's
separate wording.

277
00:16:56.190 --> 00:17:00.340 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, a temporary Central employee with two years of
such service

278
00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:03.820 line:0% position:50% align:center
falls within that stated exclusion. For other cases, check the
appointment

279
00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.480 line:0% position:50% align:center
and service status.

280
00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:10.200 line:0% position:50% align:center
For retirement Composite Transfer Grant, or CTG, DoE's 6
January

281
00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:13.220 line:0% position:50% align:center
2022 amendment is important.

282
00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:17.280 line:0% position:50% align:center
For retirement settlement, the 20-kilometre condition was
removed,

283
00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:22.100 line:0% position:50% align:center
but an actual change of residence and prescribed declaration
are required. The general

284
00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:25.000 line:0% position:50% align:center
rate is 80% of last month's basic pay, subject to the other

285
00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.440 line:0% position:50% align:center
applicable conditions.

286
00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:31.020 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, with last basic pay of Rs 50,000, eligible full
CTG

287
00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:34.570 line:0% position:50% align:center
is Rs 40,000. The order is effective from its issue date.

288
00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:38.620 line:0% position:50% align:center
For qualifying settlement to or from Andaman and Nicobar or
Lakshadweep

289
00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:42.440 line:0% position:50% align:center
island territories, the order sets CTG at 100% of last basic
pay,

290
00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:44.500 line:0% position:50% align:center
subject to its terms.

291
00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:48.420 line:0% position:50% align:center
For example, for an eligible island case with Rs 50,000 basic
pay,

292
00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.160 line:0% position:50% align:center
check Rs 50,000 at that rate.

293
00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:53.540 line:0% position:50% align:center
The rule to submit a retirement TA claim normally within 180
days

294
00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:57.140 line:0% position:50% align:center
after the journey differs from the period allowed to undertake
the move.

295
00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:03.180 line:0% position:50% align:center
Now a complete practical case. A Level 9 employee is on an
eligible official tour

296
00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:08.700 line:0% position:50% align:center
from 8 am to 5 pm that day. Eligible train fare is Rs 1,200
and

297
00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:13.440 line:0% position:50% align:center
actual non-AC city taxi is Rs 300. No free meals or duplicate

298
00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:15.330 line:0% position:50% align:center
claim is assumed.

299
00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:19.340 line:0% position:50% align:center
For nine hours, food is 70% of the Rs 1,125 reference:

300
00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:21.920 line:0% position:50% align:center
that is Rs 787.50.

301
00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:24.130 line:0% position:50% align:center
There is no hotel stay.

302
00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:28.400 line:0% position:50% align:center
Example total: Rs 1,200 plus Rs 300 plus Rs 787.50,

303
00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:32.640 line:0% position:50% align:center
that is Rs 2,287.50,

304
00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:34.880 line:0% position:50% align:center
subject to sanction and the remaining checks.

305
00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:39.390 line:0% position:50% align:center
In this case, note the return date, retain the ticket and
prescribed city-travel

306
00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:42.350 line:0% position:50% align:center
self-certification, and normally submit the claim within 60

307
00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:43.980 line:0% position:50% align:center
days after the journey.

308
00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:48.810 line:0% position:50% align:center
Example: the employee gives the office train evidence, actual
taxi details

309
00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:52.730 line:0% position:50% align:center
and the food calculation. A late claim is not automatically
approved.

310
00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:57.110 line:0% position:50% align:center
This batch focuses on official Travelling Allowance. LTC has a
separate

311
00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:00.870 line:0% position:50% align:center
reference in the guide. A full audit of the remaining
transfer, retirement and

312
00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:02.570 line:0% position:50% align:center
special cases will continue in later batches.
